  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Adds coefficient-height-aware factor-base preflight and deterministic canonical encoded/limb accounting for every retained record. Exact cumulative bytes are checked before cache insertion, exposed in progress, preserved across resumed streams, and fail closed without retaining the oversized record or its transient selected-prime group. A 262145-bit coefficient in a synthetic degree-two presentation now trips preflight instead of passing the former fixed-size estimate; the degree 2--10 exact differential suite and integrated engine remain green.",
    "risks": [
      "The mandatory arithmetic-algebra pnpm test:native gate remains intentionally pending for central integration; focused factor-base and integrated engine runtime tests, standalone Pyright, and strict-baselib receipts pass on the updated base.",
      "The selective path uses established internal Dedekind--Kummer constructors from prime_ideals.py because this lane cannot change the shared prime-ideal API; a later integration-owned public selective constructor should replace that private coupling.",
      "Preflight is deliberately conservative and may reject a plan whose eventual records would be smaller; actual incremental accounting remains authoritative and prevents underestimates from crossing max_memory_bytes."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Integration owns the pending pnpm test:native and broad build/precompile gates.",
      "Promote the selective p-maximal constructor into the shared prime-ideal API when that integration-owned surface next changes; the canonical record schema needs no migration."
